  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">promoting peaceful coexistence amongst cross border communities in Gisenyi and Goma</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at creating space and forums for constructive &#x2013; peace seeking - dialogue between Women, boys and girls from Goma and Gisenyi. Such dialogues will help remove stigma and stereotype and promote peaceful coexistence amongst Congo and Rwanda border communities. The project will be implemented by CDJP Nyundo staff and structures. Activities planned will focus on organizing conviviality days and training women and youth committees on peace themes such as conflict management, human rights, stigma and stereotypes,convention on the Prevention of Crimes of Genocide, international convention on the elimination of all forms of racial discrimination. Furthermore, different media outlets broadcasting from Goma and Gisenyi (radio, television and social networks) will be used to share specific messages, testimonies and recommendations related to peace and peaceful cohabitation, furthering therefore the project reach.</narrative>
  </description>
